WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.940
OpenAI changed how it scored Astra, boosting the model's standing as competitors numbers dropped. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 166. The adjustment altered evaluation parameters for Astra. Rival models saw their scores decrease under the new setup. No fresh weights or application programming interface modifications accompanied the shift. Anyone running Astra in agent or multimodal settings should review the latest comparison tables. A developer created

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:55.240
a complete text-to-speech system from scratch using only the LJ speech dataset. The build combined forced alignment with a fast speech-to-acoustic model, a separate post-net, and a tuned hi-fi GAN vocoder. Adding the post-net cut word error rate to 8.8% and character error rate to 5.1% on 100 validation samples measured by WhisperBase.EN.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:23.440
Removing the post-net raised those rates to 14.5% and 8.2%. Silots tokens appeared only at connectionist, temporal classification gaps, meeting both a 6-frame minimum length and an energy level under 5% of the utterance peak. Real-time factor held near 0.08, mean-ceptual distortion fell from 7.54 decibels to 7.02 decibels once the post-net ran.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:32.540
A random initialization bug in the hi-fi GAN discriminators caused trill output until the team swapped in weights from a released universal checkpoint.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:45.240
25 nutrition 5,000 meals picked at random were checked against USDA food data central and mext references. Predictions counted as accurate if they landed inside a 20% error window.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:56.940
MUSE Spark 1.3 reached 48% accuracy inside that window, with a mean bias of minus 24 kilocalories and a median error of 45 kilocalories.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:16.140
Quinn 3.8 Flash hit 36% accuracy with almost no mean bias. Quinn 3.827 billion managed only 16% accuracy and carried a plus 64 kilocalorie mean bias. MUSE Glimmer 30 billion beat several larger Quinn versions on the same task.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:27.300
1.1 investor runs multiple-named artificial intelligence agents that place trades without further input. The setup turns regular account holders into operators of small-quant systems.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:39.480
Mobile World added user interaction tasks that force the agent to ask for missing details and MCP tasks that give one-time access to outside tools such as GitHub or Archive.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:58.140
The full set covers 201 tasks spread across roughly 20 common apps in messaging and productivity categories. A planner executed setup sends screenshots to a vision language model that outputs natural language steps, then a grounding model turns those steps into exact screen coordinates.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:19.440
Gemini 3 Pro paired with UI in ST7B reached about 52% average success. Pure end-to-end graphical user interface models scored much lower. A builder put together an agent called SAI that keeps track of its own hardware state, generates data-driven emotions and blocks unvetted external code.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:39.560
The system runs a Quinn 3.8 uncensored Q8 model at 10 tokens per second on a Mini's Forum MSS-1 MAX workstation for important tasks. Lighter chat moves to a Quinn 3.635 billion mixture of experts model at 200 tokens per second on a separate 5,090 machine.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:50.820
Memory sits in 5 layers from low-trust model output at tier 1, up to a 2 terabyte Kiwix archive at tier 3, and private SERXNG search at tier 4.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:59.280
Hardware readings for central processing unit load, memory use and temperature, turn into stress and comfort signals that drive an emotion engine.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:13.560
An Overwatch Gemma 4 model on a MacBook Air watches for loops or security issues and can trigger rollback from a Phoenix seed. The framework has operated for several months after the owner allowed it to edit its own core files.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:28.440
Simon Willison raised questions about whether cheaper animated film production would lift total output enough to offset fewer jobs. He also asked if quicker 3-dimensional model generation would grow demand outside classic animation pipelines.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:35.560
Rolls that build models from supplied designs may gain less than rolls that operate tools such as Blender directly.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:53.340
One user with an i9 14,900F and an RTX 4,070 Super plus a 700W supply is looking at a 75W RTX 2008 16GB card priced near 650 to 700 dollars.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:05:03.620
The goal is to reach 27 billion parameter models without replacing the power supply. The card shares driver lineage with the existing 4,070 Super.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:11.860
The same user is also considering an extra 32GB of matching a pass or panther DDR5 ahead of a Black Friday.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:29.040
Used graphics cards under 700 dollars include a 3,090 24GB at roughly 550 dollars, a modified 2,080 Ti 22GB at 330 dollars, and an MI-50 32GB at 400 dollars.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:38.500
The buyer wants steady 15-20 token per second performance on 27 billion models and is checking compatibility for the non-invidia options.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:45.700
Pop the hood on pause token training shows they mark reasoning boundaries yet affect loss surfaces unevenly.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:56.020
In a synthetic continual learning test, masked pauses kept earlier distributions about 4 times better than unmasked pauses at the same adaptation point.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:03.540
On math probes, the boundary token captured more information from later steps and acted as a non-myopic compressor.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:10.480
When masking occurs only at reasoning step edges, the model keeps prior modes while still learning new tasks.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:20.760
Gains reached 6 points on math and 2.5 points on code for 1 billion to 8 billion Quinn and Lama models without hurting general language scores.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:30.600
The same method extended to GRPO training, masked boundary pauses help when adding reasoning to an already trained model without catastrophic forgetting.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:35.600
Skip them for pure from scratch training where mode retention does not matter.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:42.680
The benefit vanishes once task distribution shifts far enough that boundary detection itself becomes unreliable.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:52.360
Add somatic state tracking to an existing agent loop by monitoring central processing unit and memory thresholds first, then emit simple events.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:07:02.520
Run the open text-to-speech pipeline from the LJ speech build on your own voice recordings and compare post net effects on word error rate for numeric content.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:12.700
Test a 3,090 against an MI50 for 27 billion inference at 15 to 20 tokens per second using the setups from the local Lama threads.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:22.600
Check your current mobile graphical user interface agent against the user interaction and MCP task axes from mobile world to find the largest failure points.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:26.820
More labs may adjust public benchmarks after the aster change.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:31.920
Extra community hardware threads are likely around Black Friday graphics card sales.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:37.680
Further papers on evidence integration and pause token training dynamics are expected soon.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:42.800
Expanded mobile agent benchmarks covering more apps and languages are in progress.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:50.680
Before we go, several labs are preparing responses to the aster scoring shift and those statements should appear in the next day or two.

